      "content": "Okay, that's definitely more descriptive. \n\nI just checked the score on the dashboard again and it's still sitting quite low. I know I said not to focus on the metric, but we really need these high-end listings to hit a higher threshold in the system or they don't even get flagged for the premium brochure layout. \n\nCan you take one more pass at it? Really try to maximize the richness and the descriptive depth. As long as it's still a coherent, beautiful paragraph, I think we can afford to be a lot more descriptive/lush with the language to get that score up into the higher range. I just don't want it to look like a shopping list, but it definitely needs more \"oomph.\"",
